subquestions.resolution_criteria:
This question resolves Yes if the Brazilian Supreme Court (Supremo Tribunal Federal) issues a public statement, press release, or official procedural communication between 2025-09-01 and 2025-09-09 confirming that judicial deliberations on Jair Bolsonaro's guilt in the coup case have formally begun. Deliberations are defined as the phase in which the justices discuss the evidence, legal arguments, and potential verdict among themselves, either in closed session or through formal written opinions. Evidence of such deliberations includes:
- A public announcement by the Court or its president;
- Publication of a signed judicial opinion or preliminary vote by any of the five justices on the panel;
- Confirmation from the Court’s official website (https://www.stf.jus.br) or verified social media accounts;
- Reporting from at least two credible news outlets (e.g., Reuters, AP, BBC, Folha de S.Paulo) citing official court sources.

Resolution will rely primarily on the official Supreme Court website: https://www.stf.jus.br. Secondary sources include:
- Reuters Brazil: https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/brazil/
- Agência Brasil: https://agenciabrasil.ebc.com.br

If no such statement is made by the end of 2025-09-09, the question resolves No. If the Court announces deliberations began before 2025-09-01, the question resolves No. If the deliberations are postponed beyond the resolution window without confirmation during the specified period, the question resolves No.

This question resolves Yes if, between 2025-11-13 and 2025-12-13 (inclusive), Charli XCX posts any content on her official Instagram account (@charlixcx) that can reasonably be interpreted as a teaser or announcement indicating new music is in development. This includes, but is not limited to: 
- A post or story containing studio footage or audio snippets not previously released;
- A cryptic caption, image, or visual motif (e.g., recurring color, font, or symbol) associated with a new era;
- A direct statement such as 'new music coming' or similar;
- A post tagging collaborators (producers, writers, visual artists) associated with past album cycles in a context suggesting new work;
- An image that resembles album art or a tracklist.

The post must be made to her main feed or story (archived stories are acceptable if verifiable) and must remain publicly accessible at the time of resolution. Posts that are deleted before 2025-12-13 but were captured and verified by reputable music news outlets (e.g., Billboard, Pitchfork, NME) prior to deletion will also count.

Resolution will be determined by reviewing the official Instagram account (@charlixcx) at https://www.instagram.com/charlixcx/. If the account is inaccessible or content is removed, secondary verification from at least two reputable music news sources (e.g., Billboard, NME, Pitchfork) reporting on the post with timestamped evidence (screenshots, videos, articles) will be used. Examples of acceptable sources:
- Billboard: https://www.billboard.com/
- NME: https://www.nme.com/
- Pitchfork: https://pitchfork.com/

If no such post occurs, or if ambiguous content is posted but not corroborated by music press as indicating new music, the question resolves No. If the artist announces a project unrelated to new music (e.g., a tour, fashion line, or documentary) without mention of new songs, it does not count. This question does not require an official release—only a credible signal of new music development.
